{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793018584,"nonce":"aO2+v+axcoRe9v74puPl6ZpyBqQ=","title":"Studio: integrate Ashui UI inspection and composition in RayDE","message":"Status: planned; implementation has not started.\n\nProgram epic: ashui:d2286369fcac837cdeee0b0dd26c05ba2aa86bbd4c967e330ef1471f26a61c68\n\nOwn the RayDE portion of the Ashui UI Studio: .ashuiproj support, semantic Component\u003cT\u003e discovery, props/service fixtures, asynchronous compilation of unsaved source, supervised preview hosts, Code/Studio tabs, composition canvas, inspector, Edit/Presentation modes and visual changes that round-trip to authoritative Haxe documents with undo/redo and CRDT synchronization.\n\nReusable component mounting, rendering, input, inspection/source provenance and resource transport are tracked in Ashui under the program epic. This rollup is distinct from the RayScript Extension Studio (RayDE:91ad7c0fedeb255240a6d4b16105f7936a9bfc6d8162f70aef71ce257919ae8b); reuse its workbench conventions where suitable, but preview Haxe components through the chosen compiler/runtime contract.\n\nExecution gates:\n0. Rendering proof and explicit product/runtime decisions.\n1. A real mounted preview from unsaved source, with loading/error recovery.\n2. Inspection, source reveal and Edit/Presentation input.\n3. Safe visual source edits, insertion/reordering and remote browser integration.\n4. Resource/performance hardening, cross-platform CI and examples/documentation.\n\nAn associated work-item index will follow. Each item carries scope, acceptance checks and full cross-repository dependency references. Keep this rollup and the program epic open until the agreed scope and acceptance matrix are implemented and verified.","files":null}]}